  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A photograph of a Brooklyn corner near the 7th Avenue subway with a red brick building, where the trees, planters, a hydrant, bikes and a car are redrawn in flat sage and tan cartoon shapes, signed 2023.",
    "description": "A portrait format digital piece on a photograph, signed Matt Crump 2023 at lower left. A tree trunk at left rises to a canopy redrawn as flat sage, olive and grey leaf clumps with black outlines. A three storey red brick corner building with a cornice stands at centre, with the 7 Avenue Station subway entrance and a green glass kiosk at its base, and a graffiti covered wall. Two pedestrians with blank faces cross at the corner. A plum coloured cartoon car with a round window intrudes from the right. In the foreground, planters full of redrawn flat plants in olive and tan, a row of outlined bicycles, a grey fire hydrant, a cream bollard and a striped pot are drawn over the real sidewalk. The light is warm and washed.",
    "impression": "A corner in Park Slope made of paper cutouts, with the plants doing most of the acting. The tree canopy as flat clumps gives it a storybook feel and the car looks like it drove in from a different cartoon. Warm, leafy and companionable.",
